WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.420 --> 00:07.620
Another crucial element of presenting style is how you use your voice: vocal emphasis.

2
00:08.010 --> 00:14.340
Your voice can either support your message, bring it to life, and engage your audience,

3
00:14.850 --> 00:19.840
or it can let you down and undercut it. Don’t let that happen. Warm up vocally.

4
00:20.290 --> 00:29.150
What do I mean by vocal emphasis? I mean the music of your voice — not just the words, but the actual sound your voice is making.

5
00:30.150 --> 00:37.250
Is it loud? Is it soft? Is it high? Is it low? Are you pausing?

6
00:38.850 --> 00:45.120
All of these elements, the tone you bring. Think about how you might read a story to a child at bedtime,

7
00:46.890 --> 00:51.910
how you might read a simple children’s story. You’d bring it to life.

8
00:52.710 --> 01:03.200
“And then the evil wizard leaned forward and said, ‘Go down into the cellar!’”

9
01:03.720 --> 01:09.510
You’d bring it to life. Now, that may sound over the top for a business context, but I want you to try this out.

10
01:09.960 --> 01:15.300
Go home. Read your last business presentation as if you were reading it to a child.

11
01:16.290 --> 01:20.640
Record yourself on your phone. Play it back. I bet it sounds more compelling.

12
01:22.020 --> 01:28.735
Turn up the dial a little, explore, expand your vocal range, and you will engage your audience.

13
01:28.735 --> 01:33.470
Does vocal emphasis really matter? Surely words mean what they say.

14
01:34.820 --> 01:39.650
Think about this. What’s the difference between “I gave him a hundred dollars”,

15
01:41.830 --> 01:48.030
“I gave him a hundred dollars”, “I gave him a hundred dollars”,

16
01:50.410 --> 01:56.770
“I gave him a hundred dollars”? Same words. Different meaning.

17
01:57.130 --> 02:03.590
I can imagine using those sentences to answer quite different questions. Did you lend him a hundred dollars?

18
02:04.130 --> 02:08.710
Did you give her a hundred dollars? Did you give him a thousand dollars? Did you give him a thousand pounds?

19
02:09.510 --> 02:14.880
All of those I could answer with those same words, but I would emphasize differently.

20
02:15.910 --> 02:25.280
So the question of where in a sentence I put the stress, just using my voice, using the vocal emphasis, is crucial to the meaning I want to convey.

21
02:26.310 --> 02:33.090
Again, play around a bit, and think about, when you’re delivering a presentation, what’s the message you want to land?

22
02:33.890 --> 02:39.040
Where do you put the vocal weight, the vocal emphasis, that will land that message most effectively?

